# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the Epic 7 (NFR-P-5) ASan gate.
#
# Wired into the test environment by CMakeLists.txt (`LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...`)
# only when `-DRAW_RADIO_STUDIO_ENABLE_ASAN=ON`, so the Release build is unaffected.
#
# Why this file exists (the *only* suppression in the gate):
#
#   `raw_radio_studio_tests` reports a fixed, one-shot 320-byte leak whose
#   allocation stack is entirely inside fontconfig:
#
#       FcInitLoadConfigAndFonts (libfontconfig)
#         <- juce::FTLibWrapper::FTLibWrapper()   (juce_Fonts_freetype.cpp:75)
#           <- juce::Typeface::createSystemTypefaceFor(...)
#             <- rrs::brand::initialiseFonts()    (src/ui/BrandFonts.cpp:59)
#
#   JUCE creates one FreeType library + one fontconfig config per process
#   (the `FTTypefaceList` singleton, src/.../juce_Fonts_freetype.cpp:388) and
#   holds them until shutdown. fontconfig keeps process-global caches for its
#   whole lifetime and never frees them (its own `FcFini` is effectively a
#   no-op), so this is the well-known "allocate once, never free" fontconfig
#   behaviour — not a leak in raw-radio-studio, not attributable to our code, and
#   it does **not** grow per call (it is a constant, independent of session
#   length or buffer count).
#
# The suppression matches the allocation *path*, so LSan stays fully enabled and
# still fails the gate on any real leak (per-call growth) in our own code. Both
# frames below appear in every fontconfig-init leak stack; matching either is
# enough (LSan matches a frame substring of the leak's stack trace).
#
# Format: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/AddressSanitizerLeakSanitizer#suppressions
leak:FcInitLoadConfigAndFonts
leak:juce::FTLibWrapper
